outcome:
Central exposes a documented federation operator API covering four things:
- per-peer link, attestation and worker state, with the last terminal reasons (stage, reason, ioKind, elapsed time, SSH exit class) and the owned OS operations still unresolved;
- a supervised recover/re-arm action for a quarantined or failed peer, which proves the owned SSH child is reaped before reconnecting and refuses with a typed reason when it isn't;
- relay-queue visibility, meaning deferred notifications per peer with counts and last error;
- an audit record of every operator action.
No fictitious SSH accounting and no deletion of live state. Tests cover each action's success and refusal paths.
